+# OVERLAY PATCH for T08 verification. The repository copy of this file is NOT modified.
+#
+# The frame that WorldState.robot.ee_pose and every move_to_pose target refer to is
+# end_effector_link, which open_manipulator_x.urdf places at link5 + (0.1260, 0, 0). The finger
+# joints sit at link5 + (0.0817, +/-0.0210, 0) - that is 0.0443 m BEHIND the ee frame along
+# link5 -x. At the pitch these approaches actually hold, the link5 x-axis world z component is
+# about -0.60 (median -0.7327 over 204 archived approaches; -0.6016 measured at the T08
+# approach), so the fingers ride 0.0443 * 0.60 = 0.0266 m ABOVE whatever height is commanded.
+# With the box top at 0.0350 and contact_height_m 0.0200, the fingers land at ~0.0467 - 21.7 mm
+# clear of the box - so no jaw face ever contacts a side face and the motion is a friction drag
+# across the top face, which is why 44% of pushes reverse.
+#
+# This patch compensates the offset so the FINGERS, not the ee frame, reach the requested height.
+FINGER_OFFSET_COMPENSATION_M = 0.0443 * 0.60
+
